  "job_B3.2.6_20251003_114644": {
    "text": "Men \u00f0a leofestan, ure drihten \u00e6lmihtig god us singalice mynega\u00f0 \u00feurh his halgan bec mid \u00feam gastlicum\n\u00d0onne is synderlice eallum godes folce beboden, \u00fe\u00e6t hi heora gebeda lufian and \u00e6lmessan d\u00e6lan of \u00feam\nGode is la\u00f0 seo \u00e6lmesse, \u00fee bi\u00f0 mid unrihte begiten.\nAc us is mycel neod\u00feearf, \u00fe\u00e6t we ge\u00feencan, hu drihten us mid his \u00ferowunge alysde fram deofles\nFor\u00f0an we sculan weor\u00f0ian Cristes rode and biddan ure synna forgyfenessa ealle \u00e6tsomne.\nSwa he for us \u00ferowude on \u00fe\u00e6re rode and eal \u00fea sar and edwit and \u00fea heardan \u00ferowunga, \u00fee he adreah\nAc hw\u00e6t is \u00feam men betere to \u00feencenne \u00feonne embe his sawle \u00feearfe and hw\u00e6nne se d\u00e6g cume, \u00fee he\nWitodlice we magon ongitan, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea syndan uncu\u00fee, \u00fee we geseon ne magan.\nFor\u00fean we sceolan mid eallum mode and m\u00e6gne to god gecyrran and so\u00f0e bote don for urum synnum,\nGeeadmeda\u00fe eow sylfe, men \u00fea leofestan, to godes willan, \u00feonne genera\u00f0 he eow of deofles\nGe\u00feenca\u00f0 eac, \u00fe\u00e6t ge gelomlice winna\u00f0 and swinca\u00f0 and ymbe \u00fe\u00e6t sorgia\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t we urne lichaman\n\u00deonne gelimpe\u00f0 hyt \u00e6fter feawum dagum o\u00f0\u00f0e feawum gearum, \u00fe\u00e6t se ylca lichama by\u00f0 on byrgenne,\nFor\u00fean us is mycel neod\u00fe\u00e6arf, \u00fe\u00e6t we ge\u00feencan embe ure sawle \u00feearfe, \u00fe\u00e6nne heo cym\u00f0 on domes\nOft w\u00e6 habba\u00f0 gescawod, to hwilcum \u00feingum we sculan gewur\u00f0an, sy\u00f0\u00f0an we deade beo\u00f0.\nWe magan geseon, \u00feonne man binnan mynster byrgene delfe\u00f0 and \u00fea ban \u00fe\u00e6ron finde\u00f0, hwilce we\nHwar by\u00f0 \u00feonne heora wela, \u00fee hi ahtan her on life?\nAnd hi d\u00e6ghwamlice gesamnodon ma and ma tog\u00e6dere and nystan n\u00e6nigne ende, hw\u00e6nne hi \u00fe\u00e6t\nHwar com se micela heap, \u00fee him mid ferde and ymbe \u00ferungon?\nEalle \u00feas \u00feinc synd fram eagan gewitene, ne hit nu nan \u00feinc \u00fe\u00e6re sawle ne helpe\u00f0.\nAc heora lichaman licga\u00f0 on eor\u00f0an and beo\u00f0 to duste gewordene and \u00fe\u00e6t fl\u00e6sc afula\u00f0 and wirmum\nMen \u00fea leofastan, se \u00fee ges\u00e6lig bi\u00f0, he m\u00e6g hine sylfne be \u00feisse bysene l\u00e6ran.\nEac \u00fe\u00e6t gyt mare is, \u00fe\u00e6t hi scylan \u00e6fter \u00feam eor\u00f0welan edwit \u00ferowian.\nDon we \u00feonne, men \u00fea leofestan, so\u00f0e bote for urum synnum \u00fea hwile, \u00fee we on \u00feissum l\u00e6nan life syn.\nAlysan we ure sawle \u00fea hwile, \u00fee we \u00fe\u00e6t lif habban and \u00fe\u00e6t weor\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t we magan wi\u00f0 god geceapian,\nNe \u00feearf nan man \u00fe\u00e6s w\u00e6nan, \u00fe\u00e6t hyne \u00e6nig man m\u00e6ge alysan fram helle wite, gif he sylf nele his\nAc ute we beon gemyndie ure sawle \u00feearfe \u00fea hwile, \u00fee we motan \u00fe\u00e6t lif habban.\nUte gemunan \u00fe\u00e6ne egesfullan domes d\u00e6g.\nSe cym\u00f0, \u00feonne we l\u00e6st wena\u00f0, and on \u00feam d\u00e6ge we sculon for\u00f0beran swa god, swa yfel, \u00e6lc sawl be\nMen \u00fea leofestan, geearnie we, \u00fe\u00e6t ure se ytemesta d\u00e6g wur\u00f0e gode gecoren, and gecyrran we to\nNis \u00feonne nan man, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6ne deopan grund \u00fe\u00e6s hatan fyres gesecan mage, gif he wile his synna betan\nHw\u00e6t, we nu gehyrdan secgan be \u00feam \u00e6lmesfullan, hu gode sawle he h\u00e6f\u00f0, and nys n\u00e6nig man, \u00fe\u00e6t\nAnd ne bit he us nan o\u00f0er edlean, butan \u00fe\u00e6t we ure sawle swa cl\u00e6ne agifan, swa he hi \u00e6r gesceop and\nFor\u00f0an we sculan beon swi\u00f0e gemyndige godes beboda and ure sawle \u00feearfe on eallum tidum.\nAnd secgan we him \u00feanc ealra his miltsa and his eadmodnessa and his gifena, \u00fee he us forgeaf.\nAnd his naman we sculan weor\u00f0ian mid wordum and mid d\u00e6dum, and mid eallum m\u00e6gne him \u00feancian.\n\u00deonne forgif\u00f0 he us, \u00fe\u00e6t we motan to heofona rices wuldre mid blisse becuman.\n\u00dear by\u00f0 leoht and lif and englas and heahf\u00e6dras and witegan and ealle halie on drihtenes onsyne mid\n\u00de\u00e6r by\u00f0 ece gefea butan unrotnesse and geogo\u00fe butan ylde.\nNe bi\u00f0 \u00fear sar, ne gewin, ne n\u00e6nig uny\u00f0nes.\nNe \u00fear n\u00e6ni man his feond ne finde\u00f0, ne his feond ne gemet\u00e6\u00f0, ac \u00fear wunian mot, \u00fee \u00fea stowe\nMen \u00fea leofestan, ute gehyran, hu seo sawel spr\u00e6c\u00f0 to \u00feam forworhtan lichaman on domes d\u00e6g\nHeo cwy\u00f0 to \u00feam lichaman: For hwan, earma lichama, gelyfdestu on \u00fe\u00e6ne \u00fee \u00f0e eal forl\u00e6rde, \u00fe\u00e6t w\u00e6s\nHwi noldestu gelyfan \u00feinum drihtene, \u00fee w\u00e6s ahangen for us and us alysde fram helle wite?\nGehyr nu, earma lichama, \u00feu eart deofles hus, for\u00feam \u00feu deofles willan worhtest and godes lare\n\u00d0onne cwy\u00f0 seo sawel to \u00feam lichaman wependre stefne \u00feus: Wa is me nu, for\u00feam \u00fee ic \u00fea toweardan\nWa is me, for\u00feam \u00fee ic ne ondred me helle wite.\nWa is me nu, for\u00feam ic heofonan rice ne lufede.\nWa is me, for\u00feam \u00fee ic ne ondred me godes \u00feone micelan dom.\nWa me, for\u00f0am \u00fee ic ge\u00feafode eal \u00fea yfel, \u00fee \u00feu dydest.\nWa me, for\u00feam \u00fee ic sceal to helle for \u00feinum yfeld\u00e6dum and \u00feu hafast gedon, \u00fe\u00e6t ic eom deofles bearn\nHwi noldest \u00f0u gelyfan \u00feinum scrifte?\nAc seldan \u00feu gemundest \u00feine sawle.\nAc oft \u00feu gemundest, hu \u00feu o\u00f0re men beswican woldest, for\u00feam ic sceal nu to helle wite.\n\u00deonne eft cwy\u00f0 seo goda sawle to \u00feam godan lichaman: Wel \u00fee, for\u00feam \u00fee \u00feu godes cyrican\n\u00d0onne gyt cwy\u00f0 seo sawel: Wel \u00fee, gebletsode lichama, sceawa on me, to hwilcum setle \u00feu eart\n\u00dein med is on me f\u00e6ger and gesyne and \u00feu symle most eces eardes brucan on blisse.\nNe m\u00e6g nan man hit asecgan ymbe \u00fea f\u00e6gernessa, \u00fee god hafa\u00f0 gegearwod \u00feam mannum, \u00fee hine\nGod \u00e6lmihtig us la\u00f0a\u00fe to heofona rice and deofol us wile forl\u00e6ran and forl\u00e6dan to helle wite.\nGod us la\u00f0a\u00fe to life and deofol us la\u00f0a\u00fe to wite and beswice\u00f0 to dea\u00f0e.\nGod us l\u00e6re\u00f0 w\u00e6ccan and sent us on leohte heortan, \u00fe\u00e6t he wolde, \u00fe\u00e6t we oft cyrican sohtan.\nDeofol us l\u00e6re\u00f0 sl\u00e6pnesse and sent us on sl\u00e6w\u00f0e, \u00fe\u00e6t we ne magon \u00feone beorhtan beacn \u00fe\u00e6re bellan\nGod us l\u00e6re\u00f0 f\u00e6stan and \u00e6lmessan syllan earmum mannum and deofol us l\u00e6re\u00f0 oferfylle.\nGod us l\u00e6re\u00f0 cl\u00e6nnesse and deofol us l\u00e6re\u00f0 feala fule ge\u00feanc.\nGod us l\u00e6re\u00f0 eadmodnessa and deofol us l\u00e6r\u00f0 ofermodnesse.\nGod us l\u00e6r\u00f0 sibbe and wynsumnesse and deofol us l\u00e6r\u00f0 unsibbe and wrohte.\nUtan we forl\u00e6tan yfele lare and ge\u00feencan \u00feone micelan domes d\u00e6g and dimnessa helle grundes, \u00fee\n\u00dear bi\u00f0 wurma geflit and to \u00fea gristbitung.\n\u00dear bi\u00f0 unadw\u00e6sced fyr.\n\u00dear bi\u00f0 wea and wite.\n\u00dear hi sculan wunian o\u00f0 ende.\n\u00deonne is us micel neod\u00feearf, \u00fe\u00e6t we gleawlice ongitan \u00fea scortnesse \u00feysse worulde and \u00fea ecnesse\n\u00de\u00e6t ne by\u00f0 n\u00e6fre geendad \u00feam synnfullum mannum, \u00fe\u00e6t ece wite, and \u00feam so\u00f0f\u00e6stan \u00fe\u00e6t ece lif.\nFor\u00f0am swa hwilc man swa godes weorc cl\u00e6nlice and behogodlice wirce\u00f0, he bi\u00f0 ecelice gehealden.\nSe \u00fee hit \u00feonne recel\u00e6aslice and uncl\u00e6nlice wyrce\u00f0, he bi\u00f0 awyrged into helle.\nBe \u00f0am Crist cw\u00e6\u00f0: Swa hwilc man swa hine lufa\u00f0 mid cl\u00e6nre and mid inweardre heortan, he hafa\u00f0\n\u00deonne cwy\u00f0 drihten: Eala man, ic \u00fee geworhte and ic for \u00fee \u00ferowude and ic w\u00e6s a rode ahangen and\nEala man, hwar syndon \u00fea lean, \u00fee \u00feu me dydest for minre \u00ferowunge?\nNe gemundest \u00f0u na, hwilc hit bi\u00f0 on helle?\n\u00dear bi\u00f0 eagana wop and to \u00f0a geheaw.\n\u00dear bi\u00f0 unadw\u00e6sced fyr.\n\u00de\u00e6r beo\u00f0 egesfulle wyrmas, \u00fea \u00fee wundia\u00f0 and slita\u00f0 \u00fea synnfullan sawle, and \u00fea deofla drifa\u00f0 \u00fea\nAnd \u00feonne f\u00e6r\u00f0 Sanctus Petrus mid heom and byr\u00f0 on his handa helle c\u00e6ge, and nis nan deofol, ne\nAnd hi \u00feonne scylan ealle to helle wite and hi man \u00feonne in bescyf\u00f0, and Sanctus Petrus \u00fea duru\nAnd he \u00feonne weorpe\u00f0 \u00fea c\u00e6ga ofer his exle into helle.\n\u00deis he de\u00f0 \u00feonne, for\u00f0am \u00fee he ne m\u00e6g locian on \u00fe\u00e6t sar and on \u00feone micelan wop, \u00fee hi wepa\u00f0 mid\nHlud bi\u00f0 se cnyll ofer ealle eor\u00f0an, \u00feonne seo c\u00e6g fealle\u00f0 innan helle.\nAc biddan we urne drihten mid halgum gebedum and mid \u00e6lmessan, \u00fe\u00e6t he us gehealde on heofonan\nAmen.",
